[stderr] ## Optional timer and round lifecycle
[stderr] 
[stderr] Timer is an accessibility-neutral optional display mode: `off` is the default
[stderr] and tutorial always forces `off`. Starting a standard round freezes the chosen
[stderr] mode. `on` records elapsed active seconds only; it does not change selection,
[stderr] adjudication, score, streak, or availability. Pause, background interruption,
[stderr] and recovery stop elapsed time. A timeout can be emitted only for an explicitly
[stderr] enabled timer according to the separately implemented GAME-007 scoring rule.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Transition | Preconditions | Required result |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `home → selecting_theme` | Compatible cached standard package. | Show themes and timer choice defaulted to off. |
[stderr] | `selecting_theme → ready` | Valid theme and deterministic selection. | Show selected count and any shortage disclosure before start. |
[stderr] | `ready → active(card 1)` | Start accepted. | Freeze cards/revisions/package/rules/seed/timer mode into run snapshot. |
[stderr] | `active(card n) → feedback(card n)` | One valid submission or enabled-timer timeout. | Create one immutable attempt; prevent a duplicate submission from creating another. |
[stderr] | `feedback(card n) → active(card n+1)` | Continue and `n < cardCount`. | Save resolved safe boundary before showing the next unresolved card. |
[stderr] | `feedback(last) → results` | Continue after final resolution. | Commit result once; reopening is idempotent. |
[stderr] | `active or feedback → paused` | Explicit pause, background/interruption, or app shutdown at safe boundary. | Persist current safe snapshot; timer stops; no answer is inferred or submitted. |
[stderr] | `paused → active or feedback` | Resume compatible confirmed snapshot. | Restore exact card, resolved-feedback state if any, selection and timer mode; content cannot switch mid-round. |
[stderr] | `paused → recovery` | Draft corrupt/incompatible or write interrupted. | Preserve last confirmed snapshot and offer resume it, discard draft, or return home; never overwrite silently. |
[stderr] 
